# Engineering hygiene

## Size of change

- Make small, focused changes. One purpose per change.
- If a task needs a large diff, propose a split first and wait for approval.
- Do not reformat or rename unrelated code in the same change.

## Tests

- Add or update tests with every behavior change.
- Run the project's test command before saying the work is done.
- If a test fails, report it. Do not delete or weaken a test to make it pass.

## Secrets and data

- Never put secrets, tokens, keys or passwords in code, tests or comments.
- Use environment variables or the project's secret store.
- Do not paste customer data into examples. Use synthetic values.

## Explain trade-offs

- State the options you considered and why you chose one.
- Name risks and anything you did not verify.
- Say plainly when you are unsure.
